<MainLayout title="For Doubters">
  <section>
    <h2>For Doubters</h2>
    <p>Empirical Evidence consistent with the belief Afterlife phenomenon can be separated into 2 broad categories based on oft told stories of what people throughout history experienced of deceased activities.</p>
    <p>In one case, the experienced effects are localized to the site or objects at the moment of death of the deceased. In the other case, the effects can be anywhere.</p>
    <p>The first or localized, are common threads in many ghost stories. Ghosts usually appear and are localized at the site of the death or the objects associated with it.</p>
    <p>The most significant case of localized ghost story in recent times involves the Ghosts of flight 401.</p>
    <p>In this localized event, when the plane crashed, some of the spirits of 2 pilots transferred to nearby cabin instruments instead of a house. These apparently undamaged instruments were recycled into other planes in the Eastern Airlines fleet.</p>
    <p>The deceased pilots’ colleagues and passengers on instruments reported many sightings of the ghost of the 2 pilots who died in the crash.</p>
    <p>The corroborated sightings were so significant that a TV movie was made based on it. Eastern Airlines also responded by removing all the recycled equipment to stop frightening passengers.</p>
    <p>After this tragedy, there was never another fatality on any L1011 in the Eastern fleet even with subsequent accidents. Other airlines continued to have fatal accidents involving L1011 aircraft.</p>
    <p>Two subsequent Eastern L1011 flights with potentially fatal failures of engines and flight controls were miraculously landed without injuries to passengers as promised by the pilot ghosts in some prior sightings.</p>
    <p>Another not localized but direct relative of the deceased. A recent example of living/spirit interaction is from Ghosts of 9/11 which tells of a deceased father communicating with his daughter in vivid dreams but not with his surviving wife in that manner.</p>
    <p>Other stories involving the Ghosts of 9/11 is that soon after death, a spirit’s energy is at a maximum whereby it can commune with any loved ones through signs like the rustling of leaves at a particular moment, or timing occurrence of other seemingly natural event as meaningful signs of communion.</p>
    <p>In my case, that occurred the day we buried my mother. A sudden sprinkle of snow started as she was laid into the ground and the snow stopped at the end of the ceremony. A few months later, my night blooming Cereus plant which I had for several years, bloomed for the first time on her birthday and emitted an odor that matched the odor at her funeral.</p>
  </section>
</MainLayout>
